==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* [[transduco|trānsdūcō]]

===Etymology===
From {{term|trāns||across, beyond|lang=la}} + {{term|dūcō||lead|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-pronunc|trādūcō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|traduco|trādūcō|traducere|trādūcere|traduxi|trādūxī|traductum|trāductum}}

# I [[lead]], [[bring]], [[transport]] or [[conduct]] across or over something.
# I [[parade]], lead along; [[make]] a [[show]] of, [[expose]] to [[public]] [[ridicule]]; [[dishonor]], [[disgrace]], [[degrade]].
# {{context|figuratively|lang=la}} I [[transfer]], [[convert]], [[remove]].
# {{context|figuratively|lang=la}} I [[exhibit]], [[display]], [[proclaim]], [[spread]] abroad, make public.
# {{context|figuratively|lang=la}} I transfer a [[word]] from one [[subject]] or [[language]] to another; [[translate]]; [[derive]].
# {{context|figuratively|of time|lang=la}} I [[spend]], [[pass]], lead.

